# What is deliberately NOT in this repository, and why.
#
# Inputs and intermediates are out; results are in. A reader should be able to
# check every number in the README against results/*.csv without running
# anything, and reproduce the whole study from scratch with the commands in the
# Reproducing section.

# Input data: 60 MB, downloads automatically on first run (UCI HAR).
data/

# Regenerable artefacts of a run. The checkpoints are 12 trained models plus
# their per-epoch histories and prediction arrays -- binary, large, and fully
# reproduced by `python run_all.py`.
checkpoints/

# Experiment tracking stores. Local to whoever ran the study.
mlruns/
mlflow.db
mlflow.db-journal
mlflow.db-wal

# Environments and caches
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Kept on purpose, listed here so the choice is explicit rather than accidental:
#   results/raw.csv          one row per run per precision -- the evidence
#   results/summary.csv      the aggregation the README table is built from
#   results/environment.json the machine the timings were taken on
#   figures/*.png            rendered by report.py, and they display in the README
